      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town quickly became a key supply hub for placer miners along the Mokelumne River, with water channeled through ditches like Lancha Plana and Poverty Bar.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/camanche_village_california",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the late 1860s gold ran out, and Camanche fell into ghost‑town status before being flooded by Camanche Reservoir in the 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
